// Server details for the build.
//
// This file is committed with empty values so the project always generates and
// CI always builds. Put your real values in Config/Secrets.local.xcconfig,
// which is gitignored — the optional include at the bottom picks them up.
//
// Only the project reference goes here, never the full URL: xcconfig treats
// "//" as the start of a comment, so https://abc.supabase.co would silently
// become "https:". The app assembles the URL from the ref.
//
// SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF is the subdomain of your project URL.
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the anon/public key. It is safe in a client — every
// table is protected by row level security — but keep it out of git anyway.

SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF =
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =

#include? "Secrets.local.xcconfig"
